02:09:50.941 --> 02:09:52.899
corresponding data point.

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/11611-0
02:09:53.739 --> 02:09:54.739
Does that make sense?

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/11652-0
02:09:57.459 --> 02:10:03.516
We can also define some subtly different
things about these different regions.

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/11652-1
02:10:03.516 --> 02:10:08.959
You can see there's one region one which
is completely covered, right?

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/11652-2
02:10:08.959 --> 02:10:13.943
Every block within region one is a
complete block and it has its

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/11652-3
02:10:13.943 --> 02:10:15.859
corresponding data point.

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/11692-0
02:10:16.099 --> 02:10:20.120
Then we have these other regions, two,
three, and four,

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/11692-1
02:10:20.120 --> 02:10:24.428
where you have slightly different
configurations. Region 2,

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/11692-2
02:10:24.428 --> 02:10:30.099
you've got kind of the rightmost boundary
of the blocks is empty. In region 3,

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/11692-3
02:10:30.099 --> 02:10:35.699
it's the bottom most rows. So in region 2,
it's the rightmost set of columns.

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/11711-0
02:10:35.939 --> 02:10:39.917
In region 3,
it's the bottom-most set of rows that are

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/11711-1
02:10:39.917 --> 02:10:44.979
empty. And then in region 4,
which is this corner case, we have both.

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/11718-0
02:10:46.019 --> 02:10:50.499
some columns and some rows that are empty.

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/11741-0
02:10:53.539 --> 02:10:58.449
So we have to handle these slightly
differently.

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/11741-1
02:10:58.449 --> 02:11:03.459
And what it means is that as our kernels
wake up,

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/11780-0
02:11:04.419 --> 02:11:08.604
and they check what their dimension,
what their, you know, when,

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/11780-1
02:11:08.604 --> 02:11:11.694
like we talked about,
they get their unique ID,

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/11780-2
02:11:11.694 --> 02:11:16.779
and some of these unique IDs map to a
point that's actually in the data range,

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/11780-3
02:11:16.779 --> 02:11:20.899
and some of them map to points that are
outside the data range.

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/11787-0
02:11:22.819 --> 02:11:26.819
But in different ways, right,
in these regions out here.

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/11789-0
02:11:29.139 --> 02:11:29.859
That are.

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/11795-0
02:11:31.619 --> 02:11:34.339
mapping in slightly different ways.

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/11814-0
02:11:35.219 --> 02:11:41.017
But we there's so it's basically going to
cause a control flow divergence in our

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/11814-1
02:11:41.017 --> 02:11:43.379
code. We have to have like an if.

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/11857-0
02:11:46.699 --> 02:11:51.006
We have to check,
are we within the bounds of the data?

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/11857-1
02:11:51.006 --> 02:11:55.620
And if we're not,
then the thread will do something else or

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/11857-2
02:11:55.620 --> 02:12:02.002
do nothing. Okay. And what that's called,
so I'll just introduce the idea now that

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/11857-3
02:12:02.002 --> 02:12:06.539
there's this concept of a warp,
which is a set of threads.

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/11859-0
02:12:06.739 --> 02:12:08.739
That runs together.

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/11882-0
02:12:10.259 --> 02:12:17.859
And this is kind of the fundamental
parallelism of GPUs is that you have.

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/11884-0
02:12:18.819 --> 02:12:19.699
Warps.

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/11920-0
02:12:20.979 --> 02:12:26.130
is a group of threads that all run at the
same time,

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/11920-1
02:12:26.130 --> 02:12:33.321
like literally in lock step on the same
clock cycles. And so if you have,

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/11920-2
02:12:33.321 --> 02:12:38.179
and it turns out that these warps are of
size 32.

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/11921-0
02:12:38.979 --> 02:12:39.299
Okay.

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/11923-0
02:12:40.099 --> 02:12:42.459
So, that's just a...

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/11927-0
02:12:44.659 --> 02:12:46.499
Decision that was made.

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/11929-0
02:12:48.019 --> 02:12:49.059
By NVIDIA.

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/11930-0
02:12:50.899 --> 02:12:51.219
Um...

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/11947-0
02:12:52.659 --> 02:12:57.549
And not only NVIDIA, others,
I think AMD also has a warp size of 32,

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/11947-1
02:12:57.549 --> 02:13:00.099
at least on some devices, and Intel.

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/11988-0
02:13:01.579 --> 02:13:05.806
Doesn't have to be,
but that was the decision that was made

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/11988-1
02:13:05.806 --> 02:13:11.512
and it's been that way for quite a few
generations of GPUs for Nvidia and maybe,

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/11988-2
02:13:11.512 --> 02:13:15.668
I don't know if it goes all the way back
to the beginning,

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/11988-3
02:13:15.668 --> 02:13:18.979
but it goes back at least to Turing and
Volta.

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/12006-0
02:13:21.179 --> 02:13:28.499
So for now, imagine that a warp,
so in reality a warp is 32,

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/12006-1
02:13:28.499 --> 02:13:32.099
but imagine that a warp is 16.

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/12038-0
02:13:34.179 --> 02:13:40.776
Suppose a warp was 16.
So now we have these 16 by 16 blocks,

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/12038-1
02:13:40.776 --> 02:13:45.535
and so each one of these,
if a warp was 16,

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/12038-2
02:13:45.535 --> 02:13:51.699
because warps are linearized,
like in a row, contiguous.

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/12055-0
02:13:52.179 --> 02:13:58.312
threads within a warp are contiguous in
row major order.

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/12055-1
02:13:58.312 --> 02:14:01.539
So you'd have if hypothetical.

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/12058-0
02:14:02.779 --> 02:14:04.179
hypothetical warp.

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/12064-0
02:14:14.579 --> 02:14:18.819
16, real warp size 32.

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/12067-0
02:14:23.939 --> 02:14:24.499
Just for.

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/12102-0
02:14:25.699 --> 02:14:30.574
illustrative purposes,
we'll think about because it maps nicely

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/12102-1
02:14:30.574 --> 02:14:34.992
to these blocks.
Each one of these would be its own warp,

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/12102-2
02:14:34.992 --> 02:14:40.019
warp 0, warp 1, warp 2, et cetera,
all the way to warp 15, right?

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/12150-0
02:14:41.859 --> 02:14:47.178
And so now you can see what's going on
here is we have different types of warp

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/12150-1
02:14:47.178 --> 02:14:51.890
control flow divergence with these
different cases. And in group one,

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/12150-2
02:14:51.890 --> 02:14:56.333
there's no divergence.
All warps are fully occupied. In region 2,

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/12150-3
02:14:56.333 --> 02:14:59.699
we have this case where the kind of the
rightmost

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/12188-0
02:15:00.139 --> 02:15:06.022
threads in a warp are not active,
but the majority of the warp is active.

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/12188-1
02:15:06.022 --> 02:15:12.382
So actually 12 out of 16 threads in each
warp are active. Down here in group 3,

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/12188-2
02:15:12.382 --> 02:15:16.675
you've got a few warps which are
