8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/12404-0
02:17:24.339 --> 02:17:26.979
All right,
so here's an example of a kernel.

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/12411-0
02:17:28.339 --> 02:17:32.179
That converts from color RGB.

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/12449-0
02:17:33.779 --> 02:17:39.456
So A three-channel color input pixel,
each pixel has an RG and B value to

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/12449-1
02:17:39.456 --> 02:17:45.746
convert it to a single grayscale pixel,
which basically means that you apply this

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/12449-2
02:17:45.746 --> 02:17:46.819
function here.

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/12454-0
02:17:48.099 --> 02:17:51.059
You take the R, the G, and the B.

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/12501-0
