but if that kernel computes the wrong

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/17427-3
03:08:47.689 --> 03:08:51.905
answer, then it's garbage.
So if you're optimizing a function,

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/17427-4
03:08:51.905 --> 03:08:53.779
and you optimize it so much,

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/17457-0
03:08:53.939 --> 03:08:57.026
that it doesn't return the right answer
anymore,

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/17457-1
03:08:57.026 --> 03:09:01.751
then it's not doing the right thing.
So there's two things you want to do.

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/17457-2
03:09:01.751 --> 03:09:06.728
You want your function to run faster,
you want it to compute the right answer.

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/17457-3
03:09:06.728 --> 03:09:09.059
We have to always verify our results.

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/17491-0
03:09:10.819 --> 03:09:16.900
that it's continuing to compute the right
answer as we make our progressive rounds

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/17491-1
03:09:16.900 --> 03:09:21.222
of optimization.
The problem is that the same calculation,

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/17491-2
03:09:21.222 --> 03:09:25.471
if we do it on the CPU and the GPU,
may not be identical.

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/17491-3
03:09:25.471 --> 03:09:29.939
There's a bunch of reasons for this,
such as floating point,

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/17531-0
03:09:31.619 --> 03:09:38.310
is not an associative operation.
So a + b + c is not necessarily going to

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/17531-1
03:09:38.310 --> 03:09:45.725
be equal to a + b + c because of rounding
and truncation and overflow differences

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/17531-2
03:09:45.725 --> 03:09:51.059
and specific details of the IEEE
specification compliance.

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/17570-0
03:09:51.379 --> 03:09:57.815
versions and other options that you might
be able to have some control over in your

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/17570-1
03:09:57.815 --> 03:10:02.029
compiler settings and flags and things,
in some cases,

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/17570-2
03:10:02.029 --> 03:10:08.158
you may not get the same answer for the
same simple math when you run it on the

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/17570-3
03:10:08.158 --> 03:10:11.299
CPU and the GPU. So keeping that in mind,

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/17601-0
03:10:12.579 --> 03:10:19.929
We need to have verification routines
that are aware of this and instead of

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/17601-1
03:10:19.929 --> 03:10:25.151
trying to compute an exact down to the
bit agreement,

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/17601-2
03:10:25.151 --> 03:10:31.339
we have error tolerances to an acceptable
agreement within the.

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/17639-0
03:10:31.819 --> 03:10:38.739
expected deviations of all these various
different numerical precision issues that

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/17639-1
03:10:38.739 --> 03:10:42.658
exist.
So here's a recommended computation for

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/17639-2
03:10:42.658 --> 03:10:49.078
absolute and relative tolerances.
If you have a CPU result and a GPU result,

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/17639-3
03:10:49.078 --> 03:10:52.579
take the absolute value of the difference.

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/17660-0
03:10:52.859 --> 03:11:00.374
and ensure that that is less than the
maximum of your absolute tolerance or

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/17660-1
03:11:00.374 --> 03:11:06.899
your relative tolerance,
which gets scaled by the absolute value.

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/17696-0
03:11:08.499 --> 03:11:13.594
of your results.
So this is a routine you can use in your

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/17696-1
03:11:13.594 --> 03:11:18.426
error checking.
So kind of the key point is you need a

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/17696-2
03:11:18.426 --> 03:11:25.453
CPU baseline version that computes your,
you can use it both for timing and for

8cb34de9-346e-4a04-ba99-ca654a43e903/17696-3
